# MadGraph5 batch script: u u~ > mu+ mu- at LO (partonic Drell-Yan).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - Colored initial state (u u~) with a purely electroweak s-channel
#     (gamma*/Z) amplitude: exercises the initial-state colour average (1/9) and
#     the N_c colour sum on a process whose matrix element carries no alpha_s,
#     giving a fixed-coupling cross section directly comparable to an integration
#     with no coupling running.
#   - Fixed-energy partonic beams (lpp=0, u and u~ at 250+250 GeV) put
#     sqrt(s-hat) = 500 GeV well above the Z pole, so the s-channel propagator is
#     smooth (no Breit-Wigner peak to sample) — a clean 2->2 angular integral.
#
# This is the dedicated lpp=0 reference for u u~ > mu+ mu-; the PDF-convolved
# p p > l+ l- path is covered separately by the hadronic cross-section reference.
generate u u~ > mu+ mu-
output uux_to_mumu -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
